"answer": "Project Zenith is an initiative aimed at optimizing cloud storage solutions, enhancing security, accessibility, and data visualization through AI and machine learning. The project was announced for Q3 2023, with Marcus Cole as the leader and a kickoff meeting on July 15th. Key phases include design, development (led by Omar Jensen), and compliance. The team has expanded with new members Mike Chen and Lisa Ray. Milestones include a successful prototype test for secure file sharing and initial findings suggesting a 20% efficiency increase. Budgets have been approved for training ($15,000) and compliance ($55,000). An upcoming meeting on August 5th will discuss further findings."
